.TH APT-FIND-REPO 1 "January 2026" "apt-find-repo 0.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
apt-find-repo \- automatically find and configure third-party APT repositories
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B apt-find-repo
[\fB\-v\fR]
.I package
[\fIurl\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B apt-find-repo
automatically discovers and configures third-party APT repositories.
Given a package name, it searches DuckDuckGo for official repository pages,
extracts GPG keys and source entries, validates the repository, and configures
it on your system.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-v
Verbose output. Shows search queries, URLs tried, GPG key URLs, source entries,
package discovery, and installation progress.
.TP
.I package
Package name to search for. Automatically gets wildcard suffix for prefix
matching (e.g., \fBnoson\fR becomes \fBnoson*\fR to match \fBnoson-app\fR).
.TP
.I url
Optional URL of a web page containing repository installation instructions.
If omitted, performs automatic web search.
.SH FEATURES
.PP
\fBSecurity:\fR Rejects repos without GPG keys, shows its work with -v,
commits changes with etckeeper (if available).
.PP
\fBDiscovery:\fR Prioritizes official sources over how-to sites.
.PP
\fBApplicability:\fR Detects distro and arch, maps Debian to nearest Ubuntu,
maps Ubuntu non-LTS to nearest LTS as fallback.
.PP
\fBValidity:\fR Filters incompatible sources, confirms existence of requested
package in repo.
.PP
\fBModernity:\fR Writes keys to /etc/apt/keyrings/, deb822 format to
/etc/apt/sources.list.d/.
.SH EXAMPLES
Already found docs about a repo?
.PP
.nf
.RS
sudo apt-find-repo jetbrains https://github.com/JonasGroeger/jetbrains-ppa
sudo apt update
sudo apt install goland
.RE
.fi
.PP
Need help finding one?
.PP
.nf
.RS
sudo apt-find-repo tailscale
sudo apt update
sudo apt install tailscale
.RE
.fi
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/apt/keyrings/*.gpg
GPG signing keys for third-party repositories.
.TP
.I /etc/apt/sources.list.d/*.sources
Repository source entries in deb822 format.
.SH REQUIREMENTS
.TP
.B Debian-based system
Ubuntu, Debian, Pop!_OS, or similar APT-based distributions.
.TP
.B root access
Required for modifying /etc/apt/ configuration.
.TP
.B ddgr
DuckDuckGo search tool (apt install ddgr).
.TP
.B etckeeper
(optional) Automatic change tracking.
.SH SUPPORTED REPOSITORY TYPES
.IP \(bu 2
Official vendor repositories (Docker, Tailscale, Brave, etc.)
.IP \(bu 2
Ubuntu PPAs (ppa:owner/name)
.IP \(bu 2
OpenBuildService repos (build.opensuse.org)
.IP \(bu 2
GitHub-hosted APT repos
.IP \(bu 2
Self-hosted repos with standard structure
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success
.TP
.B 1
Error occurred (repository not found, missing GPG key, permission denied, etc.)
.SH NOTES
The tool requires root privileges (via \fBsudo\fR) to write system
configuration files in \fI/etc/apt/\fR.
.PP
Repository keys and sources are validated before installation. If a key or
sources file already exists at the target location, the command will fail
rather than overwrite existing configuration.
.PP
After adding a repository, run \fBapt update\fR to refresh the package cache.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR apt (8),
.BR apt-key (8),
.BR sources.list (5),
.BR ddgr (1),
.BR etckeeper (8)
.PP
For development information, see docs/CLAUDE.md in the source repository.
